    "description": "India G-sec yield-curve historical snapshots — 1Y / 5Y / 10Y / 30Y tenors. Quarterly samples (end-of-quarter close) covering the post-2014 regime. Used by the yield_curve module to backfill historical curve shapes for slope / inversion analysis. Live daily updates come from CCIL via MacroClient._fetch_gsec_curve().",
    "source_authority": "FBIL (Financial Benchmarks India Pvt Ltd) closing G-sec yields at https://www.fbil.org.in/data/G-Sec/Closing-Yields — the canonical industry benchmark used by mark-to-market and risk teams. Quarterly seed values are public CCIL/FBIL historical snapshots, cross-checked against RBI WSS Statement 25.",
    "format_notes": [
      "date is a calendar date in YYYY-MM-DD form (end-of-quarter Friday close).",
      "All yields are in percent (7.15 = 7.15%, not 0.0715).",
      "1y = 1-year T-bill / short G-sec; 5y = 5-year G-sec (belly); 10y = 10-year benchmark G-sec; 30y = 30-year long bond.",
      "Some quarters may have NULL tenors where the relevant security was illiquid (esp. 30Y pre-2016)."
    ],
    "last_updated": "2026-05-26",
    "row_count_target": "~45 quarterly snapshots covering 2014-Q1 to 2025-Q1."
  },
